WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.866
Navigation jamming and spoofing can endanger aircraft, emergency services, communications, transportation, timing, and infrastructure.

00:00:07.866 --> 00:00:19.792
Transmitting interfering or deceptive signals is heavily regulated or prohibited in many jurisdictions and can create consequences far beyond one test area.

00:00:19.792 --> 00:00:29.181
Do not build, buy, configure, transmit, test, or use jammers, spoofers, deceptive signal systems, or interference equipment.

00:00:29.181 --> 00:00:37.047
Do not attempt to locate a source through unsafe confrontation or unauthorized technical activity.

00:00:37.047 --> 00:00:43.391
When interference is suspected, prioritize safe recovery and immediate operational reporting.

00:00:43.391 --> 00:00:51.257
Notify the responsible aviation, safety, compliance, security, or operations contact according to organizational procedure.

00:00:51.257 --> 00:00:57.600
Emergency or regulatory channels may apply depending on impact and location.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:10.034
Preserve original flight logs, controller warnings, media, screenshots, timestamps, aircraft and firmware details, weather, route, crew notes, and any reports from nearby operations.

00:01:10.034 --> 00:01:15.363
Protect integrity and access, and separate observations from conclusions.

00:01:15.363 --> 00:01:22.721
Coordinate review across aviation safety, technical specialists, compliance, legal, security, and affected operations.

00:01:22.721 --> 00:01:31.602
They can determine notification, broader monitoring, equipment inspection, data validity, and whether specialized authorities should investigate.

00:01:31.602 --> 00:01:34.901
Responsible reporting avoids sensational attribution.

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:45.812
State what occurred, what safety action was taken, what evidence exists, what remains uncertain, and what operational changes are recommended.

00:01:45.812 --> 00:01:52.156
The objective is risk reduction and learning, not proving an adversary.
